# Mapping excitation-inhibition balance in schizophrenia with white-matter-microstructure informed modeling

> Whole-brain computational model fitting (EI tuning) for schizophrenia study. Fits a two-population Reduced Wong-Wang model to empirical functional connectivity (FC) using Feedback Inhibitory Control (FIC) + Excitation-Inhibition Balance (EIB) tuning.

## Project Structure
TVB-schz/
├── configs/
│   └── ei_tuning_config.yaml   ← all paths and simulation parameters
├── scripts/
│   ├── normal.sh               ← Task 1: fit SC → own FC
│   ├── shuffle_region.sh       ← Task 2: shuffled SC regions → own FC
│   └── shuffle_sub.sh          ← Task 3: SC → different subject's FC
├── tasks/
│   └── ei_tuning.py            ← main simulation script (all 3 tasks)
├── utils/
│   └── generate_shuffles.py    ← generate shuffle files (run once)
└── logs/
    ├── slurm/                  ← SLURM .out / .err per job
    ├── normal/                 ← per-subject logs for Task 1
    ├── shuffle_region/         ← per-subject logs for Task 2
    └── shuffle_subj/           ← per-subject logs for Task 3
Data and results live in $WORK/TVB-schz/ (not tracked by git).

## Data (in $WORK/TVB-schz/)
connectomes/    ← 4 weight matrix types: ADC, gFA, density, number; length matrix
data/           ← empirical FC (all subjects, all parcellations)
labels/         ← region labels per parcellation (83, 129, 234, 463, 1015)
results/        ← output .npy files (created at runtime)
shuffle/        ← shuffle permutation files (created by generate_shuffles.py)
cache/          ← tvboptim JIT cache (created at runtime)

## Three Tasks
TaskSC weightsFC targetScriptnormalsubject's ownsubject's ownnormal.shshuffle_regionsubject's own (region order shuffled)subject's ownshuffle_region.shshuffle_subjsubject's owndifferent subject's FCshuffle_sub.sh

## How to run
1. Install JAX with GPU support
```bash
conda activate $WORK/.conda/tvboptim
pip install --upgrade "jax[cuda13]"
python -c "import jax; print(jax.devices())"  # must show CudaDevice
```

2. Generate shuffle files (for tasks 2 & 3 only)
```bash
python utils/generate_shuffles.py --config configs/ei_tuning_config.yaml
```

3. Submit (should in TVB-schz/)
```bash
sbatch scripts/normal.sh
```